 This install applies to "Slicks 'N' Slide", a native Amiga port of the DOS
 shareware racing game by Timo Kauppinen. The game data is not included:
 the installer takes it from the original shareware Slix151.zip, which is
 freely available from the publisher (see Installation below).

 The port is authorized and supported by the original author, Timo
 Kauppinen. This is the full version of the game: the removal of the
 shareware limitations is authorized by the original author.


 Requirements:
 -------------
 Standalone: PAL or NTSC A1200, 68020, AGA, 2 MiB Chip RAM, AmigaOS 3.x and SetPatch.
 The WHDLoad installer requires Installer V43 or later and WHDLoad 17+.
 These system tools are not included in this archive. For standalone use,
 see the manual installation instructions below; no WHDLoad is needed.
 Close other applications on a 2 MiB machine. Allow about 1 MB free RAM for
 the extraction helper, at least 2 MB temporary disk space and 3 MB
 destination space. RAM: or RAM-backed T: may be used for temporary files
 when enough additional memory is available. Use disk on a 2 MB machine.

 The WHDLoad icon requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and 8 MiB Fast RAM.
 With 4 MiB Fast RAM, remove the icon's PRELOAD tooltype; with less, use the
 standalone game. The slave reserves 512 KiB ChipMem for the display and sound
 and runs the game in 2 MiB of Fast RAM. On a 68030 with a full MMU (not a
 68EC030), add the MMU tooltype to enable the data cache as well as the
 instruction cache. No other WHDLoad options are needed: the installed icon
 uses only the standard PRELOAD, and a Shell launch is simply:
   WHDLoad SlicksNSlide.slave
 The game reads each file in one operation and writes each saved file in one
 operation, so saving causes at most one short disk access per file.

 WHDLoad also requires a legally obtained Kickstart 3.1 image and matching
 relocation file in "Devs:Kickstarts" or "WHDCOMMON:". Supported pairs are:

   kick40063.A600  and kick40063.A600.RTB
   kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB
   kick40068.A4000 and kick40068.A4000.RTB

 Standalone play does not need WHDLoad or a Kickstart image. Neither the
 Kickstart images nor the original game data are included in this package.


 Installation:
 -------------
 Download the original shareware Slix151.zip from:

 https://www.slicksnslide.com/webapi/download.php?p=dos-slix&v=Slix151.zip

 Leave it compressed. Unpack this LHA, open its drawer and run the Install
 icon; select the ZIP when asked. The self-contained helper checks the
 supported publisher ZIP before extracting the two data files and 195 tracks.
 It never installs the DOS executable, DOSBox, configuration or a
 registration key. No host computer, UnZip utility or PC emulator is needed.

 Choose Use existing when asked about installed data to skip the ZIP and
 temporary-drawer questions and preserve modified tracks and records.
 Reinstall replaces the 195 supplied tracks and both data files.
 Updating the port keeps keys and saves. Failed extraction does not replace
 installed files. If copying fails due to disk space, retain the staging
 drawer and rerun the installer.

 For standalone installation without WHDLoad, create a destination drawer and
 run SlicksNSlideInstallData Slix151.zip <destination>/data from a Shell.
 Copy the supplied SlicksNSlide executable into data/. To update existing
 data, simply replace the native executable.


 Display:
 --------
 The original 320x200 picture is shown on a 50 Hz PAL or 60 Hz NTSC AGA
 screen, whichever the machine or WHDLoad's NTSC/PAL tooltype selects (the
 tooltype needs that monitor driver in DEVS:Monitors). The game runs at the
 same speed on both. Race physics and lap clocks run on the original
 real-time clock at any frame rate. Frames that take longer than one refresh
 are shown immediately rather than waiting for the next one, which can
 briefly tear moving objects; this happens more often at 60 Hz.


 Playing and quitting:
 ---------------------
 Double-click SlicksNSlide for WHDLoad. The installer creates one game icon.
 For standalone: CD to the installed SlicksNSlide/data drawer, then run
 SlicksNSlide from a Shell. SetPatch should have run during system startup.
 No Play script or stack increase is required. Updates remove the old Play
 script, Play.info and SlicksWHDLoad.info launch icons, but keep the game
 data.
 The installed data/ drawer holds the native executable, original data,
 tracks, configuration, driver profiles, saved championships and an optional
 SLICKS.REK. Both launch methods share these files; keep the drawer writable.

 Exit through the game's menu to save pending changes. WHDLoad's QuitKey
 (F10) exits immediately and cannot perform deferred game saves.


 Features:
 ---------
 - the complete, registered original game: single races, championships,
   shop with every weapon, demos, help, options and all eight languages
 - original graphics, fonts, tracks and sounds from the publisher's data
 - native 68020 code, AGA display and four-channel Paula sound
 - original real-time race clock at any frame rate
 - digital Amiga joysticks in both game ports


 Controls:
 ---------
 Menus: arrows, Enter, Escape; F1 for help. Configure drivers and controls in
 the original menus. Page Up/Down in menus and help: keypad 9/3, or the two
 keys immediately right of P ([ and ] on a US keyboard). Amiga Help
 replaces PC Scroll Lock for shop screenshots.
 Joystick 1 is the usual joystick port, joystick 2 the mouse port. PC
 parallel-port joystick adapters are not available on the Amiga.


 Full version and registering:
 -----------------------------
 This is the full version: every shop weapon is available, and there is no
 trial reminder or ordering screen. The removal of the shareware limitations
 is authorized by the original author, Timo Kauppinen. You can still support
 his work by registering at:

 https://www.slicksnslide.com

 The game's own ordering help (Y or F1 on the exit screen) also explains it.
 Registering gives you a personal key file, SLICKS.REK. It is optional: copy
 it into the installed SlicksNSlide/data/ drawer, next to the SlicksNSlide
 executable, and your name appears on the title screen. The same file works
 for both WHDLoad and standalone play, and reinstalling or updating keeps it.
 A key that cannot be read is ignored. This package contains no key.


 History:
 --------
 version 1.0 (02.11.2026):
 - full version: all shop items, no registration reminders or order form,
   authorized by the original author Timo Kauppinen
 - correct player helmets and option badges on the title screen
 - WHDLoad: runs the game in Fast RAM with CPU caches enabled; needs 8 MiB
   Fast RAM, or 4 MiB without the PRELOAD tooltype
 - NTSC: runs on 60 Hz NTSC machines and with WHDLoad's NTSC tooltype, at
   the same game speed and sound pitch as PAL, with the picture at the
   standard NTSC screen position

 version 0.91 (13.10.2026):
 - louder sound effects and engines
 - restored race-start sounds and synchronized traffic lights
 - removed the extra wait before driving and its effect on first-lap times
 - restored the moving start light and weapons notice
 - small gameplay performance improvements

 version 0.90 (01.10.2026):
 - initial Amiga release


